# Show Evidence When Claiming Done

When you claim that work is finished, fixed, verified, or passing, **always surface the evidence in the same response**. Do not only say where evidence lives — show it.

## Required

- **UI / UX changes:** Embed or link the relevant screenshot(s) from `evidence/` (or freshly captured paths). Prefer reading image files so they render in chat.
- **Tests / gates:** Quote the pass line(s) or attach the log file path **and** include the key result (e.g. `1 passed`, coverage %).
- **Multiple claims:** Match each claim to its evidence (rename → header screenshot; IMAP help → collapsed + expanded shots; etc.).

## Do not

- Say “done” / “fixed” / “passing” with only a prose description and no artifact.
- Point at stale evidence from before the change.
- Assume the user will open `evidence/` on their own.

## Refresh

If existing screenshots or logs predate the change, re-run the relevant check and overwrite/update evidence before claiming success.
